<h1>Summary</h1>
<p class="lede">The project in two pages: the question, the method, the three theories, and the results so far — stated plainly, including what has <em>not</em> yet been shown.</p>

<h2>The question</h2>
<p>Since Heidegger, no single thinker has produced a <em>total</em> explanatory system — one coherent account of nature, history, society, mind, and meaning together. For most of human history we had such systems; about a century ago the ambition fractured (Nietzsche, Gödel, hyper-specialization, Heidegger, the postmodern refusal). The project's hypothesis: the pace of change, the number of fields, and the density of interdependence now make a total systems theory impossible by the <strong>old method</strong> — one mind, one book — but perhaps buildable by a <strong>new</strong> one: living, distributed, plural, computationally-augmented, continuously revised. We test the hypothesis by trying to do it, using today's symptoms as the pressure-test.</p>

<h2>The method — designed disagreement</h2>
<p>The engine is a standing panel of ten reconstructed thinkers (Aristotle, Kant, Heidegger, Nietzsche, Ibn Khaldun, Braudel, Meadows, Turchin, Luhmann, Le Guin) plus twenty advisors, composed so almost every question splits the room. They argue, rate, and <strong>dissent</strong>; a chair (Claude) synthesizes the argument <em>without voting</em>; the author (Hulki Okan Tabak) ratifies; and nothing genuinely argued is ever erased. The project runs as a <strong>living document</strong> — versioned, self-correcting (a catches → learnings → rule-changes loop), disagreement-preserving, forkable — across two surfaces: <strong>this website is public</strong> (the reading surface), while the contribution repository stays <strong>private until the skeleton is stable</strong>.</p>

<h2>The thirteen pressure-tests</h2>
<p>A candidate theory earns credibility by illuminating today's condition — and by <em>drawing the arrows between its parts</em>, where "polycrisis" only lists them. The tests, in four coupled layers plus a master condition:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>M — the coherence vacuum</strong> (the loss of shared meaning; base or summit is left open).</li>
  <li><strong>Drivers:</strong> acceleration (the adaptation gap), optimization dynamics, the wealth pump / inequality, machine intelligence.</li>
  <li><strong>Dynamics:</strong> epistemic breakdown, coordination failure, institutional decay, ecological overshoot.</li>
  <li><strong>Symptoms:</strong> fertility collapse, the attention/dopamine economy, populism, anomie / loneliness.</li>
</ul>
<p>The founding seven (fertility, dopamine, propaganda, "why now," climate, coordination, populism) are all preserved inside this expanded set. It is offered as a <em>contested causal hypothesis</em>, not a settled taxonomy.</p>

<h2>The three candidate theories</h2>
<p>Not three guesses at one answer but three <em>kinds</em> — diagnosis, mechanism, response — that fit together. Each ships with its own weaknesses named in its own text, and each has been turned into a stated, falsifiable, pre-registerable claim.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>A — The Adaptation Gap</strong> (diagnostic). Today's defining condition is a widening gap <strong>G = R_c − R_a</strong> between the rate systems change and the rate humans and institutions adapt; most symptoms are downstream. <em>Best integrative reach; weakest falsifiability. Round-7 strength 7/10.</em></li>
  <li><strong>B — The Optimization Ecology</strong> (mechanistic). Self-reproducing optimizers capture human drives as fuel and run without human ends — by <strong>selection, not design</strong>. Its integrity rests on a test that distinguishes selected-to-capture from designed-to-capture. <em>Cheapest to test. 7/10.</em></li>
  <li><strong>C — Distributed Coherence</strong> (reflexive). Because no single mind can hold the whole, an adequate theory must be a governed <strong>commons of sense-making</strong>. It is turned on the project itself: does designed disagreement <em>out-catch</em> a lone author? <em>Best practice/reflexivity; most exposed to the meaning-objection. 6/10.</em></li>
</ul>
<p>The three together are an instance of the third one. Read them in full under <a href="{{ '/outputs/candidate_theories/' | url }}">the theories</a>.</p>

<h2>Results so far — honestly</h2>
<p>Across four working sessions the project has: surveyed the full <a href="{{ '/history/' | url }}">history</a> of total systems and the living contemporary field; expanded and layered the pressure-tests (7 → 13) with the cross-couplings <a href="{{ '/diagrams/' | url }}">drawn</a>; produced three rival candidate theories and <strong>operationalized all three to a falsifiable standard</strong> (each with a pre-registered first study); built the reflexive apparatus — a designed-disagreement panel, an append-to-preserve dissent log, a catches/learnings metabolism, and the Chat/Code shuttle that lets the work outgrow a single context; and stood up this public reading site while keeping the repository private. The learning loop has begun to close (a prior learning caught a live error before it shipped).</p>
<p><strong>What has not been shown:</strong> none of the three theories has yet been <em>tested</em> — the studies are specified and pre-registered but gated, awaiting a fresh ratified decision to run them. The reflexive claim (that the commons out-thinks the individual) has a designed experiment but an entangled baseline (the "panel" and the "single author" are, for now, the same underlying model). The deepest questions — whether the coherence vacuum is base or summit, whether a method can ever be a <em>meaning</em> — are kept deliberately open. The honest posture throughout: a frame you can attack precisely is worth more than one you can only admire.</p>

<h2>Where it stands</h2>
<p>Version 0.4 — foundation laid, field surveyed, three theories operationalized, the pivot to a durable repository and public site complete. The reading surface is public and evolving; the contribution repository opens for forking once the shape has settled (<a href="{{ '/docs/the_living_document/' | url }}">the living document</a>, §7). The most revealing place to start is <a href="{{ '/logs/open_questions/' | url }}">the frontier</a> — every live disagreement and open question, curated as the first thing a contributor should attack. The full record, including every dissent and every caught mistake, is on this site and, when it opens, in the repository.</p>
